[00:17.72] A carved oak table
[00:20.05] Tells a tale
[00:22.92] Of times when kings and queens
[00:25.06] Sipped wine from goblets gold
[00:29.20] And the brave would lead their ladies
[00:32.29] From out the room
[00:35.46] To arbours cool
[00:40.48] A time of valour
[00:43.49] And legends born
[00:46.45] A time when honour meant much more
[00:49.64] To a man than life
[00:52.94] And the days knew only strife
[00:55.94] To tell right from wrong
[00:59.44] Through lance and sword
[01:03.98] Why?
[01:05.94] Why?
[01:07.61] Can we never be sure till we die
[01:10.27] Or have killed for an answer?
[01:15.43] Why?
[01:17.52] Why?
[01:19.14] Do we suffer each race to believe
[01:21.86] That no race has been grander?
[01:27.17] It seems because
[01:29.59] Through time and space
[01:37.48] Though names may change
[01:39.22] Each face retains the mask it wore
[02:18.02] A dusty table
[02:20.49] Musty smells
[02:23.48] Tarnished silver lies
[02:25.60] Discarded upon the floor
[02:30.00] Only feeble light
[02:31.66] Descends through a film of grey
[02:35.93] That scars the panes
[02:41.47] Gone the carving
[02:44.22] And those who left their mark
[02:47.05] Gone the kings and queens
[02:49.45] Now only the rats hold sway
[02:53.68] And the weak must die
[02:55.47] According to nature's law
[02:59.66] As old as they
[03:04.57] Why?
[03:06.66] Why?
[03:08.22] Can we never be sure till we die
[03:11.31] Or have killed for an answer?
[03:16.15] Why?
[03:18.24] Why?
[03:19.98] Do we suffer each race to believe
[03:22.55] That no race has been grander?
[03:27.59] It seems because
[03:30.02] Through time and space
[03:37.98] Though names may change
[03:39.53] Each face retains the mask it wore
